<!--
DualShock 4 over USB: v2 (054c:09cc) and v1 (054c:05c4).

Driver: hid-playstation (kernel). Name = USB manufacturer + product string (usbhid),
version = bcdHID 0x0111 (usbhid_parse) | 0x8000 (HID_PLAYSTATION_VERSION_PATCH).

Buttons (SDL joystick index = evdev key codes in ascending order; hid-playstation
ps_gamepad_buttons): Cross (south) 0, Circle (east) 1, Triangle (north) 2,
Square (west) 3, L1 4, R1 5, L2 6, R2 7, Share/Create 8, Options 9, PS 10,
L3 11, R3 12. Axes: left stick 0/1, L2 2, right stick 3/4, R2 5. D-pad: hat 0.
The PS4 controller is handled by hid-playstation (not hid-sony) since Linux 6.2;
the image has the Raspberry Pi kernel 6.18.

deviceName is the SDL joystick name, as EmulationStation writes it. ES looks for
the GUID first and then for deviceName (InputManager::loadInputConfig), so the
name is the fallback when the version in the GUID differs (spec section 9).
The CRC in the GUID is computed from the kernel name (see guid-source).
SDL has no own name for Sony pads (controller_list.h), so the SDL name is the
kernel name. SDL_gamepad_db.h has 030000004c050000cc09000011810000 and
030000004c050000c405000011810000.

GUID with CRC (SDL 2.26 and newer, as on bookworm) and without CRC
(older SDL), computed with "emulationstation-web guid" from these values:
guid-source: bus=0x03 vendor=0x054c product=0x09cc version=0x8111 name="Sony Interactive Entertainment Wireless Controller"
guid-source: bus=0x03 vendor=0x054c product=0x05c4 version=0x8111 name="Sony Computer Entertainment Wireless Controller"

UNVERIFIED - check on hardware: Name of the v1 pad (05c4) "Sony Computer Entertainment Wireless Controller".

Sources:
  https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/blob/rpi-6.18.y/drivers/hid/hid-playstation.c
  https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/blob/rpi-6.18.y/drivers/hid/usbhid/hid-core.c
  https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/tree/release-3.2.10/src/joystick (linux/SDL_sysjoystick.c, SDL_joystick.c, controller_list.h, SDL_gamepad_db.h)
  https://github.com/RetroPie/EmulationStation/blob/stable/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp
-->
